(6) The price paid out for the materials purchased;
(7) If payment is made by check, include the check number;
(8) The signature of the customer;
(9) The applicant shall maintain and retain on the business premises, for a period of two years the names, addresses, and date of birth of all persons currently or previously employed by such applicant both full time or part time.
(Ord. of 4-6-2009(1))

307:
Every applicant operating as a scrap metal recycler within the county and any future applicants wishing to operate as a scrap metal recycler will be required to maintain records for two years and notify the county sheriff's office immediately upon receiving any of the regulated articles. Such report shall be submitted and shall contain the following information at a minimum:
